 "text": "Hi, how are you? Start with a light base color, a shade just below your skin tone, and build from there. Add small dots of warmer tones around your cheeks. Use a tone that' slightly darker than theirs, and blend it in. Don' go too light, the skin around it will look strange. No, dabs of color are much easier to control. Mix a small amount for each area. Try a small soft brush or your fingers for those. A bit of cream base under the powder helps the face look less flat.",
